WEBVTT

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:15.955
RoboICL originally reserved twelve slots for one expert

00:00:15.955 --> 00:00:19.710
demonstration and twelve for the current episode.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.110
MXI moves six of those slots to the demonstration. The

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:28.154
model sees eighteen expert windows and up to six online

00:00:28.154 --> 00:00:29.110
interactions.

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:33.292
Each window pairs two observations with the actions in

00:00:33.292 --> 00:00:36.906
between. The receipt tells the model how much of the

00:00:36.906 --> 00:00:37.670
action ran.

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:55.395
Here are two wrist images from Fill Pen Holder. In the

00:00:55.395 --> 00:00:59.064
demonstration, the right hand holds the purple pen. In the

00:00:59.064 --> 00:01:01.910
current episode, the left hand approaches it.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:06.365
Look at the red cross. The pen is beside it in the current

00:01:06.365 --> 00:01:09.974
view. The cyan edges show where the finger pads will

00:01:09.974 --> 00:01:10.390
close.

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:14.326
Later in the episode, the purple pen sits between the

00:01:14.326 --> 00:01:18.030
fingers. Both views use the same marks, even though they

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:19.750
come from different hands.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:23.484
Each wrist image keeps the camera pose from its own

00:01:23.484 --> 00:01:27.176
observation. That lets the policy relate the image to the

00:01:27.176 --> 00:01:28.990
coordinates it uses to move.

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:43.056
For an optional position estimate, the model picks the

00:01:43.056 --> 00:01:46.515
same feature in two views. Here it selected a corner of

00:01:46.515 --> 00:01:47.710
the pen holder rim.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:52.067
The rays meet at an angle of twenty seven degrees. Their

00:01:52.067 --> 00:01:55.995
closest separation is just over a tenth of a millimetre.

00:01:55.995 --> 00:01:58.870
That measures agreement between the rays.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:35.118
On 22 tasks shared with the original report,

00:02:35.118 --> 00:02:39.910
the category-balanced score rose from 52.27 to 80.58.
